<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="b4c7ee48-5bfb-5b4b-9bd7-a8f97a312c7f" activityNameId="c671beba-0436-5da9-8b85-f446c15240d2" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Toner, black, used for printing, at user</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Toner, black, used for printing, at user
This dataset relates to the mass of black toner actually printed on paper. It assumes two use cycles, i.e. one as a OEM cartridge and a subsequent as remanufactured virgin core. It is to be used to reflect black toner use in both monochrome (b/w) and colour (black pigment) laser printer systems for cartridges with a capacity of 5000 sheets and a weight of env. 1 kg including toner. An update in 2023 was done to regionalize energy and material input in the inventory; UUID: 3e580b2c-0148-3331-bf25-621aa748a235
Includes the initial OEM cartridge, the transports to the customer, the remanufacturing and disposal of spare parts and spare toner and the final disposal of the cartridge. No emissions due to printing contained.
Location: Global Electricity mix and material processing data for supplier outside Europe.
Technology: Replacement of spare parts, assembly of semifinished components.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Literature
Extrapolations: see Geography &amp; Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: None.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_3e580b2c-0148-3331-bf25-621aa748a235.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
